<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The app's privacy manifest. Add it to the app target in Xcode (File → New → File → App Privacy),
  or drag this one in and make sure it is in "Copy Bundle Resources".

  THIS FILE DESCRIBES THE APP AS IT IS BUILT TODAY, and it has to stay true as the app changes.
  Two of these answers in particular are only correct because of decisions made elsewhere:

    * NSPrivacyTracking is false because the app contains no advertising SDK, no analytics SDK and
      no third-party framework of any kind. If telemetry is ever added, it has to be declared here
      AND in the App Privacy answers in App Store Connect, and the two must agree.

    * NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes is EMPTY. The app itself collects nothing: the link token and the
      device id live in the Keychain on the device, and the wallet address is the player's own
      account identifier held by the game server, which the player created on the website — not
      something this app gathers. If you disagree with that reading, the conservative answer is to
      declare the wallet address as "Other User Content" or a user ID linked to the player; it
      costs nothing to over-declare and a mis-declaration is what gets an app pulled.

  REQUIRED-REASON APIS: the app links UserDefaults through Foundation (SwiftUI and WKWebView both
  touch it), which is a required-reason API even when your own code never calls it directly. CA92.1
  is the correct reason for an app that only reads and writes its own defaults inside its own
  container. The other required-reason categories — file timestamps, disk space, active keyboards,
  system boot time — are not used by this app's own code.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>

	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>

	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>

	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<!-- CA92.1: access only to defaults in the app's own container. -->
				<string>CA92.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
